&lt;h3 class="relative group"&gt;Deleting a Container
 &lt;div id="deleting-a-container" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 
 &lt;span
 class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;
 &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#deleting-a-container" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;/span&gt;
 
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remember to stop the container using &lt;code&gt;stop&lt;/code&gt; before deleting it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight-wrapper"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;docker rm CONTAINER_NAME&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Or&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight-wrapper"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;docker rm CONTAINER_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After deletion, you can use&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight-wrapper"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;docker ps -a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;to confirm if the container has disappeared.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Docker Notes 1 - Beginner</title><link>https://klee1611.github.io/posts/docker-operating-1.html</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jan 2020 17:06:00 +0800</pubDate><author>kourtneylee1611@gmail.com (Kuo-Hsiu (Kourtney) Lee)</author><guid>https://klee1611.github.io/posts/docker-operating-1.html</guid><description>&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;Basic Concept
 &lt;div id="basic-concept" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 
 &lt;span
 class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;
 &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#basic-concept" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;/span&gt;
 
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Docker can be seen as a simplified virtual machine (VM).&lt;br&gt;
Since it doesn&amp;rsquo;t install a full operating system, it offers a smaller footprint and faster speed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3 class="relative group"&gt;Image
 &lt;div id="image" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 
 &lt;span
 class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;
 &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#image" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;/span&gt;
 
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An Image&lt;/strong&gt; contains a lightweight runtime environment,&lt;br&gt;
including its libraries and executables.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>